    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li>Annexed by Octavian in 30 BCE, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/egypt">Egypt</a> was ruled by a prefect answerable to the emperor alone.</li><li>Its grain fed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/constantinople">Constantinople</a>, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alexandria">Alexandria</a> was a centre of trade, science and philosophy.</li><li>Christian monasticism began in its deserts, and after 451 most <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/egyptians">Egyptians</a> followed the church that became the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/coptic-orthodox-church">Coptic Church</a>.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p>Senators were forbidden to visit <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/egypt">Egypt</a> without the emperor's permission, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tiberius">Tiberius</a> rebuked his nephew <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germanicus">Germanicus</a> for touring the country in 19 CE.</p></aside>
    </section>

